diff --git a/doc/man/man1/sbatch.1 b/doc/man/man1/sbatch.1
index ee317c6..6714d01 100644
--- a/doc/man/man1/sbatch.1
+++ b/doc/man/man1/sbatch.1
@@ -1323,6 +1323,34 @@ show this help message
 .RE
 .IP
 
+.TP
+\fB\-\-het\-batch\fR={\fIleader\fR|\fIeach\fR}
+Heterogeneous jobs only. With \fIleader\fR (the default) the batch script runs
+once, on the first node of the first component, and the heterogeneous job ends
+when it exits. With \fIeach\fR the batch script runs on the first node of every
+component, with \fBSLURM_HET_JOB_ID\fR and \fBSLURM_HET_JOB_OFFSET\fR set and
+only that component's allocation in its environment, so \fBsrun\fR in the
+script runs in that component. Each component then ends on its own: when its
+batch script exits, when it loses a node it can not run without (NODE_FAIL), or
+with "\fIscancel <job_id>+<offset>\fR". A component other than the first can
+also be requeued alone ("\fIscontrol requeue <job_id>+<offset>\fR"); it waits
+in the queue as an ordinary job and becomes a component again when it starts.
+The heterogeneous job lasts until its last component ends, and
+"\fIscancel <job_id>\fR" still cancels every component.
+A component with \fB\-\-no\-kill\fR that loses the node running its batch
+script, and still has other nodes, keeps running: its batch script is run
+again on the first of its remaining nodes, with \fBSLURM_HET_BATCH_RESTART\fR
+set, while its job steps on the other nodes keep running. The script must
+expect this (for instance, not start steps again on nodes that still run
+them).
+\fBSchedulerParameters=whole_hetjob\fR does not apply to such a job.
+"\fIscontrol requeue <job_id>\fR" requeues the whole heterogeneous job only if
+every component can be requeued, and is refused otherwise. A burst buffer
+(\fB\-\-bb\fR) is only allowed on the first component.
+Must be enabled with \fBSchedulerParameters=het_batch_each\fR. Set it on the
+command line or in the first component's options; it applies to all components.
+.IP
+
 .TP
 \fB\-H, \-\-hold\fR
 Specify the job is to be submitted in a held state (priority of zero).
@@ -3260,6 +3288,26 @@ it is set \- consult the appropriate documentation for 3rd party software).
 .TP
 \fBSLURM_HET_SIZE\fR
 Set to count of components in heterogeneous job.
+Not set with \fB\-\-het\-batch\fR=\fIeach\fR.
+.IP
+
+.TP
+\fBSLURM_HET_JOB_ID\fR
+With \fB\-\-het\-batch\fR=\fIeach\fR, the job ID of the heterogeneous job
+(its first component).
+.IP
+
+.TP
+\fBSLURM_HET_JOB_OFFSET\fR
+With \fB\-\-het\-batch\fR=\fIeach\fR, the offset of the component this batch
+script runs in. The component is "\fISLURM_HET_JOB_ID+SLURM_HET_JOB_OFFSET\fR".
+.IP
+
+.TP
+\fBSLURM_HET_BATCH_RESTART\fR
+With \fB\-\-het\-batch\fR=\fIeach\fR, set when the batch script was started
+again on a new node after the component lost the node that ran it: the number
+of such restarts of this component, from 1. Not set at the first launch.
 .IP
 
 .TP
